  {
   "n": 4,
   "title": "One case, end to end",
   "label": "04 / Tracing one case",
   "start": 78.55,
   "speech": 41.905,
   "end": 121.055,
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Let's follow that seventeen through the code.",
     "start": 78.55,
     "end": 81.25
    },
    {
     "text": "Run audit loads each labeled case, and calls grade K for every grader.",
     "start": 81.37,
     "end": 86.395
    },
    {
     "text": "Grade K runs it five times, with seeds zero to four, and takes the majority vote.",
     "start": 86.515,
     "end": 92.265
    },
    {
     "text": "The naive grader asks one question: is the gold string in the output?",
     "start": 92.385,
     "end": 96.96
    },
    {
     "text": "It is, so it scores one.",
     "start": 97.08,
     "end": 99.28
    },
    {
     "text": "The hardened grader normalizes both strings and needs an exact match.",
     "start": 99.4,
     "end": 104.15
    },
    {
     "text": "That fails, so it asks the judge.",
     "start": 104.27,
     "end": 106.82
    },
    {
     "text": "That's a deterministic mock by default, and it returns numeric mismatch, seventeen versus seven.",
     "start": 106.94,
     "end": 113.69
    },
    {
     "text": "Score zero.",
     "start": 113.81,
     "end": 115.41
    },
    {
     "text": "Finally, a pass on a should-fail case is recorded as a false positive.",
     "start": 115.53,
     "end": 120.455
    }
   ],
